b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 662.0 Td (Q.1 \(a\) State and prove the Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion for three finite sets A,) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 648.5 Td (     B, and C. [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 635.0 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 621.5 Td (Formula:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 608.0 Td (|A U B U C| = |A| + |B| + |C| - |A n B| - |B n C| - |A n C| + |A n B n C|) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 594.5 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 581.0 Td (Step-by-step Proof:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 567.5 Td (1. Let D = B U C. Then A U B U C = A U D.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 554.0 Td (2. By two-set inclusion-exclusion: |A U D| = |A| + |D| - |A n D|.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 540.5 Td (3. Substitute D = B U C:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 527.0 Td (   |A U \(B U C\)| = |A| + \(|B| + |C| - |B n C|\) - |A n \(B U C\)|) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 513.5 Td (4. By distributive law: A n \(B U C\) = \(A n B\) U \(A n C\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 500.0 Td (5. Apply two-set rule to |\(A n B\) U \(A n C\)|:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 486.5 Td (   |\(A n B\) U \(A n C\)| = |A n B| + |A n C| - |\(A n B\) n \(A n C\)|) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 473.0 Td (                       = |A n B| + |A n C| - |A n B n C|) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 459.5 Td (6. Substitute back into step 3:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 446.0 Td (   |A U B U C| = |A| + |B| + |C| - |B n C| - \(|A n B| + |A n C| - |A n B n C|\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 432.5 Td (               = |A| + |B| + |C| - |A n B| - |B n C| - |A n C| + |A n B n C|. \(Proved) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 419.0 Td (    \)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 405.5 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 392.0 Td (Numerical Example:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 378.5 Td (In an MCA class of 100 students: 60 know Python, 50 know Java, 40 know C++. 30 know P) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 365.0 Td (    ython & Java, 20 know Java & C++, 25 know Python & C++, and 15 know all three.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 351.5 Td (Total knowing at least one language:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 338.0 Td (|P U J U C| = 60 + 50 + 40 - 30 - 20 - 25 + 15 = 90 students.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 324.5 Td (Students knowing none of the three = 100 - 90 = 10 students.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 311.0 Td () Tj
b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 297.5 Td (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 284.0 Td (Q.1 \(b\) What is an Equivalence Relation? Verify if relation R on Integers defined by ) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 270.5 Td (    a R b <=> \(a - b\) is divisible by 5 is an equivalence relation. [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 257.0 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 243.5 Td (A relation R on set S is an Equivalence Relation if and only if it satisfies:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 230.0 Td (1. Reflexive: a R a for all a in S.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 216.5 Td (   Here: a - a = 0 = 5  0, which is divisible by 5. Hence Reflexive.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 203.0 Td (2. Symmetric: If a R b, then b R a.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 189.5 Td (   If \(a - b\) = 5k \(k in Z\), then \(b - a\) = -\(a - b\) = 5\(-k\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 176.0 Td (   Since -k is an integer, \(b - a\) is divisible by 5. Hence Symmetric.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 162.5 Td (3. Transitive: If a R b and b R c, then a R c.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 149.0 Td (   If \(a - b\) = 5k and \(b - c\) = 5m, then:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 135.5 Td (   \(a - c\) = \(a - b\) + \(b - c\) = 5k + 5m = 5\(k + m\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 122.0 Td (   Since \(k + m\) is an integer, \(a - c\) is divisible by 5. Hence Transitive.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 108.5 Td (Conclusion: Since R is Reflexive, Symmetric, and Transitive, R is an Equivalence Rela) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 95.0 Td (    tion.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 81.5 Td () Tj
