b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 527.0 Td (Q.5 \(a\) State and prove the Handshaking Lemma in Graph Theory. [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 513.5 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 500.0 Td (Statement: In any undirected graph G = \(V, E\), the sum of degrees of all vertices equ) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 486.5 Td (    als twice the number of edges:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 473.0 Td (sum\(deg\(v\)\) = 2  |E| for all v in V.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 459.5 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 446.0 Td (Proof:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 432.5 Td (1. Every edge e = \(u, v\) connects two vertices u and v.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 419.0 Td (2. When calculating deg\(u\), edge e is counted once.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 405.5 Td (3. When calculating deg\(v\), edge e is counted once again.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 392.0 Td (4. Hence, each edge contributes exactly 2 to the sum of degrees of vertices in G.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 378.5 Td (5. Therefore, sum_{v in V} deg\(v\) = 2  |E|. \(Proved\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 365.0 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 351.5 Td (Corollary: In any undirected graph, the number of vertices with odd degree is always ) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 338.0 Td (    EVEN.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 324.5 Td (Proof: Total sum is 2|E| \(even\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 311.0 Td (sum\(deg\(v\)\) = sum_{v is even}\(deg\(v\)\) + sum_{v is odd}\(deg\(v\)\) = Even.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 297.5 Td (Since sum of even degrees is even, sum of odd degrees must also be even.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 284.0 Td (Sum of odd integers can only be even if the count of terms is EVEN.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 270.5 Td () Tj
