b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 297.5 Td (Q.9 \(a\) Explain Null Hypothesis, Type I and Type II errors with real-world examples. ) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 284.0 Td (    [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 270.5 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 257.0 Td (1. Null Hypothesis \(H0\): Statement of status-quo or no significant effect. Example: ") Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 243.5 Td (    A new machine does not increase production speed.") Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 230.0 Td (2. Alternative Hypothesis \(H1\): Statement that contradicts H0.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 216.5 Td (3. Type I Error \(Alpha Error\): Rejecting H0 when H0 is actually TRUE \(False Positive\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 203.0 Td (    .) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 189.5 Td (   Example: Convicting an innocent person in court.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 176.0 Td (4. Type II Error \(Beta Error\): Failing to reject H0 when H0 is actually FALSE \(False ) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 162.5 Td (    Negative\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 149.0 Td (   Example: Letting a guilty criminal walk free.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 135.5 Td (5. Level of Significance \(alpha\): Usually set to 0.05 \(5%\) or 0.01 \(1%\).) Tj
